    "pressure": {
      "file": "mechanical_cartridge_seal_pressure.glb",
      "title": "A micro-thin film seals across the faces",
      "description": "Springs and the hydraulic closing force press the rotating face against the stationary seat. Liquid from the chamber (outside diameter) forms a film of only ≈ 0.5–1 µm between the lapped faces, and its pressure falls across the face width to atmosphere at the inside diameter. Balance ratio (≈ 0.7–0.85 for balanced seals) sets the face load. The flush (Plan 11: from discharge to the seal chamber) removes heat and keeps the faces cool; running dry destroys the faces in seconds. A cartridge is pre-assembled and pre-set, so installation errors are fewer — but the setting clips must be removed before start-up.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
